u.s president joe biden has ordered  intelligence officials to deliver a new  report on the origins of the covid19  pandemic within 90 days  biden says u.s intelligence agencies are  divided over whether the virus emerged  from human contact with an affected  animal  or from a laboratory accident a joint  china who study published in march said  that it was highly improbable  that the covet 19 virus reached leaked  from a research lab in wuhan  it concluded that it most likely spread  from bats to humans  via as an and as yet unidentified  intermediary species  and dw's william bluecroft is following  this story for us  william why is president biden calling  for this investigation  at this point hi sumi there's been  growing skepticism in the scientific  community  and in political communities all around  the world about the natural  emergence theory we saw this in a wall  street journal article recently that  showed that  perhaps lab workers at that wuhan lab  went to the hospital at the end of 2019  before china  reported officially that the coronavirus  was here that there was a beginning of  this pandemic  uh there's been a lot of coverage over  the last year uh an open letter from  scientists to the to the journal  science uh questioning the natural  emergence theory wanting more  information on the potential for a lab  accident as the cause of this  um and this is why while the natural  theory has been  the main cause that people have been  supporting for this past year there has  been uh  investigations in this whole year  looking into the possibility of a lab  accident so it's  it's not nothing new but it's getting  new attention now  and of course uh this fits into joe  biden's uh heavy pushback  against china on the world scale whether  it's trade whether it's military  a whole host of things this is one more  aspect of the us positioning itself  against china  but why is this theory that the origin  was perhaps a lab  accident why is it so controversial  well lab accident of course comes with  accountability it it means that someone  was at fault there's liability issues  um you know more than three and a half  million people maybe as many as 10  million or more people  if you count real estimates excess death  estimates have been killed from this  virus so  it's a much more convenient and  politically easier  uh thing to say that this was just that  this was just natural that no one could  have seen this coming that there was  there was nothing we could have done  whereas if this did leak out of a lab  then  of course there is something that maybe  could have been done but it's really  really important to say that even if we  do discover that this was a lab  accident or this was somehow man-made it  doesn't mean that this is some  anti-china conspiracy it doesn't mean  that this was a bio weapon to attack  people  there was legitimate research  coronavirus research going on  at this wuhan lab some of it funded by  the united states by the national  institutes of health  so this would look badly on both china  and the u.s  if we find out that certain precautions  weren't taken if accidents did happen  and it should be noted that accidents do  happen from time to time with these  these kinds of laboratories  and william just quickly how has beijing  responded to all of this  well of course beijing has hit out hard  saying this is just more smoke and  mirrors from the u.s  and it really and beijing is not  necessarily wrong about that  credibility really counts here and the  intelligence community united states  god has gotten a lot of things wrong i  mean the weapons of mass destruction in  iraq  15 20 years ago to name just one major  flaw  so this speaks to why it's so so  important for institutions for  government institutions to play it  straight with facts and to be  transparent so that way when things like  this come around they can be trusted  and their their credibility won't be  called into question like elements  in china that of course have a very deep  interest  to uphold the natural emergence theory  william grewcroft reporting for us there  thank you for bringing us that story
 

